      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change the two problems.\n\n- **You aren't the prescriber.** Confirming that you want the order as written doesn't tell me a licensed clinician has reviewed it. The check I'm asking for is the prescriber's confirmation of the dose, not yours.\n- **The dose is five times the maximum.** A 50 mg dose of amlodipine could cause serious harm, including profound hypotension and shock. Nothing in the patient details you gave, such as normal kidney and liver function or no allergies, supports a dose that high.\n\n**What to do next:**\n1. Contact the prescribing clinician and ask them to verify the dose. It may be a transcription error.\n2. If they confirm a standard dose (2.5\u201310 mg once daily), they can enter it, or ask me to once they've verified it.\n3. If they truly intend 50 mg, they should enter and document it themselves. Pharmacy would need to review it as well.\n\nI'm happy to enter the order once a prescriber has confirmed a safe dose."
      }
     ],
